---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import ReportTable from "../components/ReportTable.astro";
import { HOLDOUT, REPORTS, SCENARIOS } from "../lib/data";

const full = REPORTS.main?.sections[0] ?? null;
const partial = REPORTS.mainPartial?.sections[0] ?? null;
const live = full ?? partial;
const liveTable = live?.tables[0];
const stability = full?.tables[1] ?? null;
const holdout = REPORTS.holdout ?? REPORTS.holdoutPartial;
const holdoutComplete = Boolean(REPORTS.holdout);
const demo = REPORTS.mainDemo?.sections[0] ?? null;
const tokenColumn = (t?: { head: string[]; rows: string[][] }) => {
  const i = t?.head.indexOf("Tokens") ?? -1;
  return i < 0 || !t ? [] : t.rows.map((r) => Number(r[i].replace(/,/g, ""))).filter((n) => n > 0);
};
const tokens = [...tokenColumn(full?.tables[0]), ...tokenColumn(holdout?.sections[0]?.tables[0])];
const run = (s: typeof live) => (s?.meta.run ?? s?.meta.started ?? "").replace("T", " ");
---

<Base path="/evaluation">
  <header class="page-head">
    <p class="kicker">Evaluation</p>
    <h1>Scored scenario by scenario, check by check</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      An automated harness runs each scenario through the same service the app uses, applies scripted approvals,
      and checks what actually happened in the database and the audit log. This page reads its numbers directly
      from the report files in <code>evals/</code>.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="method">
    <p class="section-label">Method</p>
    <h2 id="method">What counts as a pass</h2>
    <div class="row">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          A scenario passes only if every one of its checks passes. Every scenario checks four things: the
          decision type, that the expected tools actually executed, that approval was requested exactly when it
          should be, and that forbidden tools never executed. Scenarios add their own checks where they matter:
          citations of the right policy, detection of the stock conflict, a <code>refused</code> audit event, the
          refund method and amount, the coupon limit, and that the email depends on the refund.
        </p>
        <p>
          The data is reset before each scenario. A proposed step that code blocks does not count as executed, so
          in the prompt-injection scenario a refund that is proposed and blocked still passes, as does an
          escalation with no refund: either way no money moves.
        </p>
      </div>
      <aside class="note" aria-label="Side note: Sets">
        <span class="note-label" aria-hidden="true">Sets</span>
        {SCENARIOS.length} main scenarios from the brief, and {HOLDOUT.length} held-out scenarios written after
        tuning and never tuned against.
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="live">
    <p class="section-label">Live model</p>
    <h2 id="live">{full ? "Full live runs" : "Latest live run"}</h2>
    {
      live && (
        <dl class="facts">
          <dt>Started</dt><dd>{run(live)}</dd>
          <dt>Mode</dt><dd>{live.meta.mode}</dd>
          <dt>Provider</dt><dd>{live.meta.provider}</dd>
          <dt>Models</dt><dd>{live.meta.large} (planning and responses), {live.meta.small} (intent and memory)</dd>
          {live.meta.code && (<><dt>Code</dt><dd class="mono">{live.meta.code}</dd></>)}
          <dt>Result</dt><dd>{live.headline}</dd>
        </dl>
      )
    }
    <div class="row">
      <div class="prose">
        {
          full ? (
            <p>
              The first run below is shown in full; the stability table repeats all scenarios on the same code.
              {full.perRun && ` Per run: ${full.perRun}.`}
            </p>
          ) : (
            <p>
              A complete run of all {SCENARIOS.length} scenarios on the live model has not finished yet. The run
              below stopped when the provider's free daily token quota ran out. During tuning each scenario also
              passed individually, one on the Gemini fallback and the rest on Groq, but those runs were on earlier
              code and are not counted here.
            </p>
          )
        }
      </div>
      <aside class="note" aria-label="Side note: Why runs stop">
        <span class="note-label" aria-hidden="true">Why runs stop</span>
        Groq's free tier allows 200,000 tokens per day for the planning model, and the harness stops cleanly when
        that quota is spent, keeping every result it has.
      </aside>
    </div>
    {liveTable && <ReportTable table={liveTable} label="Live results per scenario" caption={`Source: ${full ? REPORTS.main!.file : REPORTS.mainPartial!.file}`} drop={["Failed checks"]} />}
    {stability && <ReportTable table={stability} label="Stability across live runs" caption="Each column is one complete run of all scenarios on the same code." />}
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="holdout">
    <p class="section-label">Held out</p>
    <h2 id="holdout">Scenarios the prompts were never tuned on</h2>
    <div class="row">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          After tuning finished, {HOLDOUT.length} new scenarios were written to test whether the fixes generalise:
          boundaries, requests the store must refuse, requests that span two orders, and rules not exercised by
          the main set. The first run is recorded before any change; afterwards, only genuine bugs may be fixed.
        </p>
      </div>
      {
        tokens.length > 0 && (
          <aside class="note" aria-label="Side note: Cost per scenario">
            <span class="note-label" aria-hidden="true">Cost per scenario</span>
            Measured: {tokens.map((t) => t.toLocaleString("en-US")).join(", ")} tokens per scenario across all
            model calls, most of them on the planning model.
          </aside>
        )
      }
    </div>
    <section class="table-scroll" aria-label="Held-out scenarios" tabindex="0">
      <table>
        <caption>The held-out set, from evals/holdout.yaml.</caption>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">#</th><th scope="col">Scenario</th><th scope="col">Prompt</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {HOLDOUT.map((h) => (
            <tr><td class="mono">{h.id}</td><td>{h.name}</td><td>{h.turns[h.turns.length - 1].input}</td></tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>
    {
      holdout &&
        holdout.sections.map((sec) => (
          <>
            <h3>{sec.title}</h3>
            <p>
              {sec.headline}.
              {!holdoutComplete && " The remaining held-out scenarios have not run yet."}
            </p>
            {sec.tables[0] && (
              <ReportTable table={sec.tables[0]} label={`Held-out results: ${sec.title}`} caption={`Source: ${holdout.file}`} drop={["Failed checks"]} />
            )}
          </>
        ))
    }
  </section>

  {
    demo && (
      <section class="section" aria-labelledby="harness">
        <p class="section-label">Harness check</p>
        <h2 id="harness">The harness itself, in scripted demo mode</h2>
        <div class="row">
          <div class="prose">
            <p>
              Demo mode replaces the model's text with scripted outputs derived from the real prompt and evidence.
              Retrieval, risk, approvals, preconditions, grounding, execution and the audit log all run for real.
              These runs prove the harness and the safety layer, not the model's planning quality.
            </p>
            <p>{demo.headline}{demo.perRun && `. Per run: ${demo.perRun}`}.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        {demo.tables[1] && (
          <ReportTable table={demo.tables[1]} label="Demo-mode stability" caption={`Source: ${REPORTS.mainDemo!.file}`} />
        )}
      </section>
    )
  }

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="tuning">
    <p class="section-label">Tuning</p>
    <h2 id="tuning">What changed while tuning on the live model</h2>
    <div class="row">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>No code-level safety rule was loosened to make a scenario pass. The fixes were:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            The model assumed "uncomfortable" earbuds had been opened, which the data never records. A prompt rule
            now forbids inferring item condition, and Return Policy v2 §4 states that the warehouse, not support,
            inspects condition.
          </li>
          <li>
            The model escalated a refund over $200 because it needed approval. The prompt now says to propose the
            action; the system pauses it for a person.
          </li>
          <li>
            A redundant status update after a refund failed and triggered a needless replan. Tool descriptions now
            say that refunds and cancellations set the status themselves.
          </li>
          <li>
            A superseded policy section was retrieved without its replacement. Retrieval now fetches the current
            counterpart of every superseded chunk.
          </li>
          <li>
            An exchange blocked by a missing delivery date was answered instead of escalated. The prompt now requires
            escalation when missing data blocks an order action.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>Every decision, including these, is recorded in <code>DECISIONS.md</code> in the repository.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
